# Store every file exactly as it is on disk.
#
# This is not the usual advice, and it is deliberate.  main_window.py is
# UTF-8 with a BOM and CRLF endings; other modules are LF.  Letting git
# normalise line endings would rewrite those files on checkout, and a BOM
# that moves or a CRLF that becomes LF is the kind of change that breaks a
# build without showing up as anything readable in a diff.
* -text

# Binary, so git does not try to diff or merge them
*.png binary
*.pdat binary
*.adat binary
*.cdat binary
*.ddat binary
*.step binary
*.pdf binary
